## Implementing an Interface

### Step-by-Step

1. Define the interface
2. Define your type
3. Write the impl block
4. Provide all required methods

```xiom
pub interface Greet {
  fn greeting(self: &Self) -> Str;
}

pub type User = { name: Str; }

impl Greet for User {
  fn greeting(self: &User) -> Str {
    return "Hello, " + self.name + "!";
  }
}
```

### Implementing Multiple Interfaces
```xiom
pub type Counter = { value: Int; }

impl Display for Counter {
  fn to_str(self: &Counter) -> Str {
    return "Counter(" + self.value.to_str() + ")";
  }
}

impl Eq for Counter {
  fn equals(self: &Counter, other: &Counter) -> Bool {
    return self.value == other.value;
  }
}

impl Default for Counter {
  fn default() -> Counter {
    return Counter{ value: 0 };
  }
}
```

### Generic Implementations
```xiom
impl Display for Vec[T]
  where T: Display;
{
  fn to_str(self: &Vec[T]) -> Str {
    var s = "[";
    for i in 0..self.len() {
      if i > 0 { s = s + ", "; }
      s = s + self[i].to_str();
    }
    s = s + "]";
    return s;
  }
}
```

### The Compiler Checks
- ALL required methods are implemented
- Method signatures match exactly
- No missing methods

